==Strategy==

This is a very angel-heavy stage, so anti-angel units like [[Rocker Cat (Rare Cat)|Ramen Cat]] will help immensely.

Bring some anti-red units such as [[Crazed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Whale Cat]] to deal with the Bore, as it spawns early on in the stage. Save up money for the Bore before it spawns so you can adequately control it.

Once the base is hit, fire the cat cannon to disrupt the Gabriels from clipping into your frontline. Lure the Boraphim near your base to separate it from the Sleipnir and then start spamming all of your anti-angel and dps units. Angel crowd controllers like [[Juliet Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Juliet the Maiko]] and [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]] can cripple Boraphim and ease pressure on the frontline. Once Boraphim is slowed/frozen, [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] can quickly melt it down.

If you choose not to lure the Boraphim, be mindful of the Sleipnir, as it can destroy your melee/midranger stack if you push too hard. For this reason, it is a good idea to bring something that can outrange the Sleipnir like [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun Wolf]] to provide additional support in case this happens.

